  "markscheme": {
    "html": "<section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"a.i\"><p><strong>a.i</strong></p><p>Correct readoffs Δx = 3 m, cΔt = 1 m ✓ (Δs)<sup>2</sup> = «1<sup>2</sup> − 3<sup>2</sup> =» −8 m<sup>2</sup> ✓   Ignore units as they are not required for the answer. Do not award MP2 if the answer is positive.</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"a.ii\"><p><strong>a.ii</strong></p><p>Does not depend on/is independent of the reference frame OR Is the same according to every «inertial» reference frame ✓   Do not allow vague answers that describe quantities that don’t change.</p>\n<p>Events P and Q occur simultaneously in an inertial reference frame S′. The clocks of S and S′ are synchronized at <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x=x'=0\"></span>.</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"b.i\"><p><strong>b.i</strong></p><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x'\"></span> correct ✓ ct′ consistent with their <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x'\"></span> ✓    Lines must start at origin. Allow a tolerance of ± 1 small grid square at the end of each line.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_02\"><img alt=\"Source markscheme diagram 2\" src=\"asset:fig_02\"/></figure></p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"b.ii\"><p><strong>b.ii</strong></p><p>«<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{v}{c}=\\frac{1}{3}\"></span> so» <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v=0.33c\"></span> or <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.0\\times 10^{8} m s^{-1}\"></span> ✓   Watch for ECF from bi. Allow fraction as the answer, i.e. <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{c}{3}\"></span></p></section>"
  },
  "paper": "paper_2",
  "question": {
    "html": "<section class=\"context\"><p>The space–time diagram shows the coordinate axes (<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x\"></span>, ct) of an inertial reference frame S. Two events, P and Q, are plotted.<br/><br/></p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"a.i\"><p><strong>a.i</strong> Calculate the space–time interval (Δs)<sup>2</sup> between P and Q. [2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"a.ii\"><p><strong>a.ii</strong> (Δs)<sup>2</sup> is an invariant quantity. Outline what is meant by an invariant quantity. [1]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b.i\"><p><strong>b.i</strong> Sketch, on the diagram, the coordinate axes (<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x'\"></span>, ct′) of S′. [2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b.ii\"><p><strong>b.ii</strong> Determine the speed of S′ relative to S. [1]</p></section>"
